  "question": {
    "text": "The area (in sq. units) in the first quadrant bounded by the parabola, $y=x^{2}+1$, the tangent to it at the point (2,5) and the coordinate axes is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "7Zp0d",
      "text": "$\\frac{8}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4HCK8",
      "text": "$\\frac{37}{24}$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "FLIiE",
      "text": "$\\frac{187}{24}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "5SumT",
      "text": "$\\frac{14}{3}$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/fYoggIIYGTN6xBD6Qx3VBLkKetcriHuvr-bQe0fp3es.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nThe equation of parabola $x^{2}=y-1$\r\n\r\nThe equation of tangent at (2,5) to parabola is\r\n\r\n$y-5=\\left(\\frac{d y}{d x}\\right)_{(2,5)}(x-2)$\r\n\r\n$y-5=4(x-2)$\r\n\r\n$4 x-y=3$\r\n\r\nThen, the required area\r\n\r\n$=\\int_{0}^{2}\\left\\{\\left(x^{2}+1\\right)-(4 x-3)\\right\\} d x-$ Area of $\\Delta A O D$\r\n\r\n$=\\int_{0}^{2}\\left(x^{2}-4 x+4\\right) d x-\\frac{1}{2} \\times \\frac{3}{4} \\times 3$\r\n\r\n$=\\left[\\frac{(x-2)^{3}}{3}\\right]_{0}^{2}-\\frac{9}{8}=\\frac{37}{24}$",
    "image": null
  },
